[dvystrcil/gpu-batch] n8n-lane-a job ends in FileNotFoundError writing status.json  (model=qwen3-coder-next:latest, 36s, lane=claude)
## Why
The `n8n-lane-a` job in `gpu-batch` keeps failing with a `FileNotFoundError` when trying to write `/work/TEMPLATE/status.json.1`. This prevents the batch lane from completing successfully and blocks downstream CAD batch processing.

## What we know
- Pod `n8n-lane-a-20261107t074604-k88z7` is in `Error` state with exit code 1 ([live pods](https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1941)).
- Logs show `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/work/TEMPLATE/status.json.1'` in `/opt/gpu-batch/gpu_batch/runner.py`, line 85 ([logs](https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1941)).
- The error occurs during `job.write()` when calling `tmp.write_text(...)` ([runner.py:85](https://github.com/dvystrcil/gpu-batch/blob/main/gpu_batch/runner.py#L85)).
- A sibling pod `n8n-lane-a-20261107t074604-r2-4j4fg` completed successfully, indicating the issue is not systemic to the entire lane.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] **AC1.** The `n8n-lane-a` job completes without `FileNotFoundError` when writing status files.
- [ ] **AC2.** The `/work/TEMPLATE` directory exists and is writable by the job container before `job.write()` is called.
- [ ] **AC3.** A test job in `gpu-batch` verifies that status.json files can be written to `/work/TEMPLATE`.

## Lane
claude — the failure is in Python runner code (`runner.py`) and likely involves missing directory setup or race conditions in volume mount timing; requires inspecting job manifest and runner logic to determine root cause.

